Sale Supply Stock Difference
============================

Adds "Purchase Only the Shortage" to the product's Supply On Sale policy.
When a sale creates its customer shipment, available physical stock is reserved
first. A purchase request is created only for the remaining unreserved quantity,
rounded up to the purchase unit's precision. Future receipts do not count as
available stock. Reprocessing the sale does not duplicate purchase requests.

The standard Never, Stock First and Always policies remain unchanged. Direct
supplier-to-customer shipments continue to request the full quantity.
